CONTENT = {'home_intro': '<h1>A little practice.<br><em>A lot of progress.</em></h1><p>Start with a keyword. Take on a full paper.<br>Build the practice you need, at your own pace.</p>', 'home_extra': '', 'about': '<div class="eyebrow">ABOUT YOUR STUDY SPACE</div><h1>Practice with purpose.</h1><p>RE Revi is an independent GCSE Religious Studies practice resource for Eduqas Route A: Component 1, Component 2 Christianity and Component 3 Islam. It is not an official Eduqas website.</p><h2>Questions and marking</h2><p>Questions are selected from an existing bank; no AI creates or marks your answers. Part A uses key concepts from the official glossary. B, C and D use past-paper questions with matching indicative content. Generated D instructions use the Summer 2026 guidance; links to the historical originals are retained.</p><p>Self marking is guidance, not an official examination result. Accurate alternative answers may receive credit. Exact band tables are provided as official PDF extracts. The latest full public schemes incorporated are Summer 2025, with updated D guidance for 2025/26.</p><p>Optional SPaG scoring is offered only on 1(d) in Components 1 and 2. The actual examination allocates these marks; switching them off is a practice setting.</p><h2>Your answers and privacy</h2><p>By default, typed answers and self marks are kept only in your browser’s session storage. They normally survive a page refresh in the same tab. Closing the tab normally removes them, although browser session recovery can restore them. Use “Save answers” to keep a copy, and “Clear this practice” on a shared device. If browser storage is unavailable, your work remains only in the current page.</p><p>Downloading a question PDF sends the selected question identifiers to this server. Your typed answers are not sent when downloading that PDF. Feedback emails open in your own email application and are only sent by you. Long answers can be downloaded and attached manually.</p><h2>Optional answer-sharing links</h2><p>If you explicitly choose “Make a link to share my answers”, a snapshot of the questions, typed answers, self marks and optional name is uploaded to this server. Your teacher’s email address is not included. Anyone with the unguessable link can view it without an account, so only include information you want to share.</p><p>You choose a lifetime of 1, 7, 14 or 29 days. Access ends at the displayed expiry time. An hourly cleanup removes expired snapshots; the maximum 29-day lifetime leaves a buffer so stored answer data is deleted within 30 days. Expired links are also removed when accessed. Shared answer files are excluded from database backups and access logs do not record sharing-page URLs. You can delete the snapshot early using “Delete shared answers” in the tab that created it. If you clear or close the tab, automatic expiry still applies.</p><p>Clearing your browser practice does not delete an existing sharing link. Copies that a recipient downloads, prints, emails or otherwise saves are outside this server’s deletion process.</p><p>We use essential cookies for security, private access when enabled, and admin login. We use no analytics or advertising trackers, and load no third-party fonts or scripts. Nginx access logs include IP address, requested URL and timestamp and rotate daily with 14 rotations retained. Service diagnostic logs follow the server’s retention policy. Cloudflare provides the public connection and processes connection information under its own policies.</p><h2>Administration</h2><p>Admin accounts manage questions and keyword definitions. Administrative records and import history are retained in the database and encrypted transport is required. For support, content corrections, privacy enquiries or account requests, email <a href="mailto:rerevi@zafirshirazi.com">rerevi@zafirshirazi.com</a>.</p><h2>Official sources</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.eduqas.co.uk/qualifications/religious-studies-gcse/#tab_pastpapers" rel="noreferrer">Eduqas qualification and past papers</a></li><li><a href="https://www.eduqas.co.uk/media/shqhzosf/eduqas-gcse-rs-route-a-gft-from-2016-300924.pdf" rel="noreferrer">Route A Guidance for Teaching</a></li><li><a href="https://www.eduqas.co.uk/media/foveuosu/eduqas-newsletter-summer-2026-gcse-religious-studies.pdf" rel="noreferrer">Summer 2026 assessment guidance</a></li><li><a href="https://www.eduqas.co.uk/media/5dtfofos/how-to-mark-a-d-question-2025_.pdf" rel="noreferrer">Updated D marking guide</a></li><li><a href="https://resources.eduqas.co.uk/pages/ResourceSingle.aspx?rIid=737" rel="noreferrer">Official key concepts glossary</a></li></ul><p>Source questions and mark schemes © WJEC Eduqas.</p><p>RE Revi was inspired by <a href="https://re.ibzz.uk" rel="noreferrer">re.ibzz.uk</a>. Use it alongside RE Revi as part of your revision.</p>', 'footer': '<span>RE Revi · Independent practice resource</span><span>Source questions and schemes © WJEC Eduqas. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy & sources</a> · <a href="mailto:rerevi@zafirshirazi.com">Support</a></span>'}

